<title>RUSSIA: Russia centre sees 96 aluminium output off 0.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Russia centre sees 96 aluminium output off 0.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian production of primary aluminium this year will be 0.7 percent lower than in 1995, the government's Centre for Economic Trends said.</p>
<p>It issued the following forecasts in the government bulletin published on Tuesday. Forecasts for non-ferrous metals did not include absolute figures, only percentage changes.  </p>
<p>PRODUCTION OF NON-FERROUS METALS</p>
<p>    PERCENTAGE CHANGE FROM YEAR EARLIER   1996    1995</p>
<p>    Alumina					   -5     +15</p>
<p>    Primary aluminium			     -0.7    +4</p>
<p>    Rolled aluminium			     -39	-0.2</p>
<p>    Copper in copper concentrate	     -21	+6</p>
<p>    Refined copper				  +2     +15</p>
<p>    Nickel					    -8     +19</p>
<p>    Zinc						+3     +21</p>
<p>--Jonathan Lynn, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
